{# The logins a delegate may use: their team's accounts and the shared roles.
   Included in the access sheet and written to /etc/pelab/logins.md. #}
{% set team = pelab_workspace_teams[item] | default('') %}
{% set teammates = (pelab_workspace_teams | dict2items | selectattr('value', 'equalto', team) | map(attribute='key') | sort) if team else [item] %}
## Your team's logins{{ (' (' ~ team ~ ')') if team else '' }}

In this lab you may sign in as a teammate, or as the platform team, to play that
role: for example to review your own change as a teammate when you work alone,
or to approve your team's environment request as the platform team. At work you
never would: accounts are personal, and a shared login defeats every control you
see this week.

| Who | User | Password | For |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
{% for name in teammates %}
| {{ 'You' if name == item else 'Teammate' }} | `{{ name }}` | `{{ pelab_delegate_passwords[name] }}` | Workspace https://{{ name }}.{{ pelab_domain }}, Gitea, Harbor |
{% endfor %}
| The platform team | `{{ pelab_platform_approver_user }}` | `{{ pelab_platform_approver_password }}` | Gitea only: approves pull requests to platform/environments (Day 3) and platform/policies (Day 5) |
| Everyone (read-only) | `{{ pelab_viewer_user }}` | `{{ pelab_viewer_password }}` | Argo CD and Grafana |

**Switching user, the easy way:** keep your own login in your normal browser
window, and open a **private window** for the other user (Edge and Chrome:
Ctrl+Shift+N, on a Mac Cmd+Shift+N; Firefox: Ctrl+Shift+P, on a Mac Cmd+Shift+P).
Sign in there as the teammate or as `{{ pelab_platform_approver_user }}`, do the review, and
close the private window. To be a third person, sign out in the private window
(top-right menu → Sign Out) and sign in again.
